  "articleBody": "VIP buyer lists can seem like a golden ticket to exclusive properties in places like Palm Beach, Boca Raton, or West Palm Beach. And they can be! But, like anything, there are common mistakes to watch out for to make sure you're getting the real deal and not just a lot of noise. You want to make sure the information you receive is truly valuable and relevant to your luxury home search.\n\nCommon Mistakes to Avoid\nFirst off, steer clear of lists using stale or purchased contact data. You want timely, accurate info, not old leads. Similarly, if you're getting messages without documented permission, that's a red flag. Reputable agents always get your explicit consent. Another common issue is failing to remove unsubscribed recipients – good lists respect your choices. Also, be wary of exaggerated claims about exclusivity or availability. Not every property can be ",
